---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const sections = [
  { id: 'overview', label: 'Overview' },
  { id: 'what-we-collect', label: 'What we collect' },
  { id: 'device-only-settings', label: 'Device-only settings' },
  { id: 'notifications', label: 'Notifications' },
  { id: 'no-tracking-or-analytics', label: 'No tracking or analytics' },
  { id: 'third-party-services', label: 'Third-party services' },
  { id: 'childrens-privacy', label: "Children's privacy" },
  { id: 'data-retention-and-deletion', label: 'Data retention and deletion' },
  { id: 'data-protection-officer', label: 'Data Protection Officer' },
  { id: 'changes-to-this-policy', label: 'Changes to this policy' },
  { id: 'contact-us', label: 'Contact us' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — GraceSoft Proverbs"
  description="A plain-language account of what GraceSoft Proverbs does and doesn't collect."
  page="privacy"
>
  <div class="legal-wrap">
    <div class="legal-header">
      <span class="eyebrow accent">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: 8 August 2026</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-notice">
      This policy is a drafted starting point and has not yet been reviewed
      by a lawyer. Treat it as a plain-language description of intent, not
      as legal advice, until that review has happened.
    </div>

    <nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        {
          sections.map((s) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.label}</a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <div class="legal-body">
      <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
      <p>
        GraceSoft Proverbs is built around a simple idea: the app should
        work fully on your device, with nothing sent anywhere. This policy
        explains, plainly, what that means for your data — which, in
        short, is that we don't collect any.
      </p>

      <h2 id="what-we-collect">What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        We do not collect, receive, or have access to any personal
        information through the app. There is no account to create, no
        sign-in, and no server that the app talks to for its day-to-day
        reading experience. All five translations and all reading themes
        are bundled into the app at install time, so reading a chapter
        never sends a request anywhere.
      </p>

      <h2 id="device-only-settings">Device-only settings</h2>
      <p>
        Preferences — your chosen translation, reading theme, font size,
        serif/sans setting, verse-number visibility, and notification
        time — are stored locally on your device only. We never see these
        values, and they never leave your device unless you back up or
        transfer your device using your platform's own backup tools,
        which are governed by Apple's or Google's privacy practices, not
        ours.
      </p>

      <h2 id="notifications">Notifications</h2>
      <p>
        The optional daily reading reminder is scheduled entirely on your
        device using your operating system's local notification
        scheduler. The app requests notification permission only at the
        moment you turn the reminder on — never on first launch, and
        never for any other purpose. No notification content or schedule
        is transmitted to us or to any third party.
      </p>

      <h2 id="no-tracking-or-analytics">No tracking or analytics</h2>
      <p>
        The app contains no analytics software development kit, no crash
        reporter that phones home, no advertising identifier, and no
        third-party tracking library. We do not know how often the app is
        opened, which translation is most read, or anything else about
        how you use it. This microsite follows the same rule: no
        analytics or tracking scripts run on any of its four pages.
      </p>

      <h2 id="third-party-services">Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        Installing the app involves the App Store or Google Play, which
        collect their own installation and purchase data under their own
        privacy policies — that data is between you and the platform, not
        something we receive. This website is served as static files with
        no backend of its own; loading the <code>fonts.googleapis.com</code>
        fonts (Playfair Display and Montserrat) is handled per Google's own
        privacy practices, not ours.
      </p>

      <h2 id="childrens-privacy">Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Because the app collects no personal information from anyone,
        there is nothing collected from children either. The app and this
        site are not directed at collecting information from any age
        group, by design rather than by an age gate.
      </p>

      <h2 id="data-retention-and-deletion">Data retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        There is nothing on our servers to retain or delete, because there
        is no server-side storage of your data in the first place.
        Deleting the app removes every setting stored on your device
        along with it — there is no account to separately close and no
        remote copy of your preferences to request the deletion of.
      </p>

      <h2 id="data-protection-officer">Data Protection Officer</h2>
      <p>
        Davina Leong is the Data Protection Officer for GraceSoft Proverbs
        and is the named contact for any privacy-related request, question,
        or complaint — including requests to access, correct, or delete
        personal data under applicable data protection law. As noted above,
        we hold no personal data on our servers to begin with, so most such
        requests will simply confirm that. Reach the DPO directly at <a href="mailto:davinaleong@gracesoft.com">davinaleong@gracesoft.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="changes-to-this-policy">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the "Last updated" date at the top of this
        page will change with it. Because the app has no way to push
        notices to you directly, meaningful changes will also be reflected
        on this page's Home section and, once available, in the app's own
        release notes.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact-us">Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:davinaleong@gracesoft.com">davinaleong@gracesoft.com</a>. See the <a href="/support">Support</a> page for other ways to
        reach us.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
